  "id": "6",
  "content": "# Review provider and model in graph-manager's Start run form\n\n## What to build\n\nThe engine now has `--review-provider <name>` and `--review-model <m>`. They set the provider and model of every reviewer that does not name its own. The fixer keeps the run's provider and model. Expose both flags in graph-manager:\n- in the run options schema (server);\n- as two fields in the Start run drawer (web);\n- in the command preview;\n- in the saved per-workspace run defaults;\n- through the `open_start_run` MCP tool, which already accepts `options: runOptionsSchema`, so it follows automatically.\n\nFor a sandboxed start, add the review provider to the providers whose logins are copied into the container.\n\nUI:\n- **\"Review provider\"**: a `<select>` with \"Same as run\" (empty value) followed by the providers (the same list as the Provider control, `fake` shown as \"fake (test)\").\n- **\"Review model\"**: a text input with placeholder \"Same as run\", validated like Model (\"One word, not starting with -\").\n\nBoth go in the main area right after the Model / Concurrency row, in their own `start-run-numbers` row.\n\n## Context: files to read before implementing\n\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runoptions.ts` (62 lines):\n  - `runOptionsSchema` (L5-17; `model: z.string().max(200).regex(/^[^\\s-]\\S*$/, \"must be a model name\").optional()`)\n  - `optionArgs(o)` (L21-34): args in a fixed order: `--no-merge`, human-review, `--model`, `--concurrency`, …\n  - `RESERVED_FLAGS` (L37)\n  - `startArgs` (L59-62)\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/runs.ts`: L15 `PROVIDERS`; L17-24 `startBody`; L100 `args = startArgs(...)`; L113-117 sandbox start with `providers: [body.provider]`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/internal.ts` L38 and L148: the `--sandbox` terminal path picks `--provider` out of the args and uses `providers: [scan.provider]`. Also pick `--review-provider`. `RUN_VALUE_OPTIONS` from `graph-execution/api` now contains `--review-provider` and `--review-model`.\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/sandbox.ts` ~L576: the providers list (run provider + enabled reviewers' providers).\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/runOptions.ts`:\n  - `RunOptionsForm` (L5-17), `RunOptionsBody` (L20-32), `emptyForm` (L34-46)\n  - `FormErrors` (L48)\n  - `MODEL` regex (L56)\n  - `formErrors` (L66-81)\n  - `optionsOf` (L86-111)\n  - `formOf` (L114-135)\n  - `optionLines` (L138-153), which must follow the server order\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunOptionsFields.tsx` (119 lines):\n  - the `input(key,label,testId,{placeholder,...})` helper (L51-76)\n  - the Model/Concurrency row (L90-93): `<div className=\"start-run-numbers\">{input(\"model\",\"Model\",\"start-run-model\",{placeholder:\"Provider default\"})}{input(\"concurrency\",...)}</div>`\n- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/StartRunDrawer.tsx`:\n  - L11-14 `PROVIDERS` / `PROVIDER_OPTIONS`; `RunOptionsFields` must not import from StartRunDrawer (circular), so move `PROVIDERS` / `PROVIDER_OPTIONS` to a small `web/providers.ts` and re-export them from StartRunDrawer\n  - the `<select>` example for Workspace (L357-371): `<label className=\"field\"><span className=\"field-label\">Workspace</span><select className=\"select mono\" value=… onChange=… data-testid=\"start-run-workspace\">`\n  - `commandPreview` (L38-45)\n- Tests:\n  - `server/routes/runoptions.test.ts`: a fake bin writes argv.json; `HEAD=[\"diamond\",\"--spec\",\"spec.md\",\"--provider\",\"fake\"]`; `expect(await argv()).toEqual([...HEAD, \"--no-merge\", ...,\"--web\"])`\n  - `server/runoptions.test.ts`\n  - `web/runOptions.test.ts`\n  - `web/pages/StartRunDrawer.test.tsx` L126-145: fills fields, compares the preview with `commandPreview(...)`, and parses the POST body\n  - `server/tools/open-start-run.test.ts` L83-86\n\n## Step-by-step tasks\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runoptions.ts` (+ tests)\n- **IMPLEMENT**: `reviewProvider: z.enum(PROVIDERS-with-fake).optional()` (import the list so it stays derived from the catalog; avoid an import cycle with routes/runs.ts by moving `PROVIDERS` to a tiny `server/providers.ts` if needed) and `reviewModel` (same rule as `model`). In `optionArgs`, emit `--review-provider <p>` and `--review-model <m>` right after `--model`. Add both flags to `RESERVED_FLAGS` so extra args cannot repeat them.\n\n### UPDATE `routes/runs.ts`, `routes/internal.ts`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: For sandboxed starts, `providers` = the run provider + the review provider (deduplicated).\n\n### UPDATE web: `web/providers.ts` (new), `runOptions.ts`, `RunOptionsFields.tsx`, `StartRunDrawer.tsx`\n- **IMPLEMENT**:\n  - Form fields `reviewProvider: string` (`\"\"` = same as run) and `reviewModel: string`.\n  - Errors: `reviewModel` uses the model rule.\n  - `optionsOf` sets only non-empty values; `formOf` reads them back loosely, ignoring an unknown provider.\n  - `optionLines` emits them in the server order.\n  - The UI row with test ids `start-run-review-provider` and `start-run-review-model`.\n\n### UPDATE tests\n- `runoptions.test.ts` (route): options `{ reviewProvider: \"fake\", reviewModel: \"m\" }` → argv `[...HEAD, \"--review-provider\", \"fake\", \"--review-model\", \"m\", \"--web\"]`.\n- `runoptions.test.ts` (schema): `reviewProvider: \"nope\"` is a 400.\n- `web/runOptions.test.ts`: errors, `optionsOf`, `formOf`, `optionLines`.\n- `StartRunDrawer.test.tsx`: choosing \"codex\" in Review provider and typing \"o3\" in Review model shows `--review-provider codex --review-model o3` in the preview and posts `options: { reviewProvider: \"codex\", reviewModel: \"o3\" }`.\n- `open-start-run.test.ts`: `options: { reviewProvider: \"claude\" }` is accepted and lands in the prefill.\n\n### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/README.md`\n- **IMPLEMENT**: L201 (the Start run option list): add \"review provider and review model (reviewers only; the fixer keeps the run's)\".\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Start run shows \"Review provider\" (default \"Same as run\") and \"Review model\".\n- [ ] Starting a run with them passes `--review-provider` / `--review-model` to the engine, in that order after `--model`.\n- [ ] `open_start_run` with `options.reviewProvider` preselects it.\n- [ ] A sandboxed run with a different review provider copies both providers' logins.\n- [ ] `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` pass.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run build -w graph-execution\nnpm run typecheck && npm run lint\nnpm test -w graph-manager -- src/server/runoptions.test.ts src/server/routes/runoptions.test.ts src/web/runOptions.test.ts src/web/pages/StartRunDrawer.test.tsx src/server/tools/open-start-run.test.ts\n```\n",
  "dependencies": [
